hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1717","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya who said: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam who said: News was conveyed to us by Ibn Farrukh.\n\nAnd narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah who said: Narrated to us 'Amr ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tariq who said: News was conveyed to us by 'Abdullah ibn Farrukh who said: Narrated to me Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of 'Ata', on the authority of Anas ibn Malik (RA), who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the one who prayed the least lengthy prayer while still completing it.\""\n\nHe said: \""I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" and when he would give the salutation"","" he would stand up immediately.\""\n\nThen I prayed with Abu Bakr (RA)"","" and when he would give the salutation"","" he would spring up from his place as if he were standing from hot stones.\""\n\n'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Rahman did not mention: \""He was the one who prayed the least lengthy prayer.\""\n\nAbu Bakr (RA) said: \""This is a rare narration; it was not narrated by other than 'Abdullah ibn Farrukh.\""\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
